{
  "$comment": [
    "The contract between internal/filter (compiles to SQL) and web/src/filter (evaluates",
    "against the replica). Both test suites load this file; neither computes the expected",
    "answer, so a change that makes both implementations agree on something wrong still",
    "fails.",
    "",
    "Expected ids are compared as a SET, sorted ascending. Ordering is a display option and",
    "is tested separately — mixing the two here would make an ordering change look like a",
    "filter regression.",
    "",
    "evaluatedAt fixes the clock so relative dates ('-10d') are reproducible. Resolving them",
    "at save time instead is the bug this pins: a view called 'Updated this week' that means",
    "the week it was saved in.",
    "",
    "SHORT NAMES. Inside 'values' and 'expect', 'e1' or 'a11' is shorthand for the full id",
    "  01900000-0000-7000-8000- + leftPad(name, 12, '0')",
    "so 'e1' is ...-0000000000e1 and 'a11' is ...-000000000a11. Both loaders expand the same",
    "way. Written out in full these arrays are unreadable, and an unreadable fixture is one",
    "nobody checks when it disagrees with them.",
    "",
    "See docs/03-architecture/06-filter-grammar.md."
  ],

  "evaluatedAt": "2026-08-15T12:00:00Z",
  "timezone": "Europe/Lisbon",

  "relativeTokens": {
    "$comment": [
      "Every relative token, and the exact instant it resolves to at the evaluatedAt above",
      "in the timezone above. Both suites resolve each token through their own real code",
      "path and compare against these strings.",
      "",
      "This table exists because the case list above structurally cannot catch a token that",
      "only one evaluator has heard of: a case using such a token fails on the side that",
      "rejects it, so nobody writes one, so the divergence is invisible to exactly the",
      "mechanism built to prevent it. That is not hypothetical — the client shipped `now`,",
      "`yesterday`, `tomorrow`, `startOfMonth` and `startOfYear`, the server refused all",
      "five, and a filter the bar built could be used and then not saved.",
      "",
      "It also pins something the id sets cannot: agreeing on WHICH ISSUES match is weaker",
      "than agreeing on WHICH INSTANT, because with seven issues a great many wrong instants",
      "select the right rows. Every value here is a UTC instant, so the timezone arithmetic",
      "is part of what is being compared and not part of the comparison.",
      "",
      "2026-08-15 is a Saturday. Lisbon is UTC+1 in August and UTC+0 in January, which is",
      "why startOfYear is the only midnight here that is also midnight in UTC — and why a",
      "resolver that treated the offset as constant would fail on that line alone.",
      "",
      "Everything except `now` is the START of a day. `now` is the clock itself: it is the",
      "one token that names an instant rather than a day, which is what makes `dueDate <",
      "now` mean overdue."
    ],

    "now":          "2026-08-15T12:00:00Z",
    "today":        "2026-08-14T23:00:00Z",
    "yesterday":    "2026-08-13T23:00:00Z",
    "tomorrow":     "2026-08-15T23:00:00Z",
    "startOfWeek":  "2026-08-09T23:00:00Z",
    "startOfMonth": "2026-07-31T23:00:00Z",
    "startOfYear":  "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",

    "-7d": "2026-08-07T23:00:00Z",
    "+3d": "2026-08-17T23:00:00Z",
    "+2w": "2026-08-28T23:00:00Z",
    "-1M": "2026-07-14T23:00:00Z",
    "-1y": "2025-08-14T23:00:00Z"
  },

