    {
      "$comment": [
        "The next three pin whitespace, which is where the two evaluators drifted apart.",
        "",
        "The server folds with search_fold — lower(unaccent(x)) and nothing else — and then",
        "matches with LIKE. The client used ~/store's fold, which also collapses runs of",
        "whitespace and trims the ends, because that fold exists for title ORDERING and for",
        "the trigram index, where collapsing is right. Applied to contains it silently",
        "rewrote the needle, so a filter matched on screen and returned nothing from the",
        "API — the shape of bug a saved view shows you and a digest email does not.",
        "",
        "Recorded with the SERVER's answer deliberately. search_fold is baked into the",
        "IMMUTABLE expression of two GIN indexes on the busiest table in the product, so",
        "changing that side means a REINDEX; and trimming a needle is the wrong semantics",
        "anyway. Somebody who types a trailing space meant the trailing space."
      ],
      "name": "a trailing space in the needle is part of the needle, not noise to be trimmed",
      "filter": { "field": "title", "op": "contains", "values": ["redirect "] },
      "expect": []
    },
    {
      "name": "a leading space likewise — ' the' is not 'the'",
